{"blocks":[{"content":"Synthesis of blast-radius ordering with evidence grounding:\n\nThe PARKED.md identifies six gaps. The RESULTS.md evidence that 44 checks were vacuous, evadable, dead, or absent, and that ~160 checks proved failable under ~590 reverted mutations, confirms that guard-death defects are the recurring failure class. The ordering is:\n1. _reset() guard (digest corruption) — append-only record integrity\n2. Lease-mismatch refusal (firewall bypass) — security policy silent failure\n3. Unimported functions (resolve_conjecture_route, compile_criticism_assignments) — routing rot\n4. Context receipt recovery guard — recovery path failure\n5. Torn-tail repair gate — partial coverage exists, marginal gap\n6. Census delta (11 vs 14) — observability discrepancy\n\nThe key countercondition for Priority 1 is whether WorkflowReplayState.digest is downstream-consumed (SCR_005, SCR_006). If not, Priority 1 may drop. The key countercondition for Priority 2 is whether the lease-mismatch refusal is the sole enforcement site or has defense-in-depth. The key countercondition for Priority 3 is whether the functions are dead code.","handle":"SCR_001","possible_next_move":"Resolve SCR_005/SCR_006: check whether WorkflowReplayState.digest is consumed by any downstream integrity check. This determines whether Priority 1 holds or drops.","was_aimed_at":["SRC_001"],"why_keep_this":"This synthesis grounds the ordering in the evidence and makes the counterconditions explicit, so a maintainer can implement test 1 tomorrow and know exactly what would falsify the priority assignment."},{"content":"Refined blast-radius ordering with countercondition gates:\n\n1. _reset() guard — CRITICAL: append-only record corruption. Countercondition: is WorkflowReplayState.digest downstream-consumed? (SCR_003)\n2. Lease-mismatch refusal — HIGH: security policy bypass. Countercondition: is the guard redundant with another tested layer?\n3. Unimported functions — MODERATE: routing rot. Countercondition: are they dead code or transitively tested?\n4. Context receipt recovery guard — MODERATE: recovery path silent failure. Countercondition: is the guard redundant?\n5. Torn-tail repair gate — LOW: partial coverage exists. Countercondition: does test_torn_append.py already cover it?\n6. Census delta (11 vs 14) — LOW: observability discrepancy. Countercondition: is it by design?\n\nEach priority has a falsifiable countercondition that would drop it. This makes the ordering criticizable, not dogmatic.","handle":"SCR_002","why_keep_this":"The countercondition gates make the ordering a set of testable hypotheses rather than assertions, aligning with the Popperian framework."},{"content":"Regression test ordering by blast radius:\n\n1. _reset() guard (digest corruption) — append-only record integrity\n2. Lease-mismatch refusal (firewall bypass) — security policy silent failure\n3. Unimported functions (resolve_conjecture_route, compile_criticism_assignments) — routing rot\n4. Context receipt recovery guard — recovery path failure\n5. Torn-tail repair gate — partial coverage exists, marginal gap\n6. Census delta (11 vs 14) — observability discrepancy, unexplained\n\nKey principle: what corrupts the append-only record outranks what hides a refusal, which outranks what hides a routing failure, which outranks what hides a recovery failure, which outranks partial coverage gaps, which outranks unexplained observations.","handle":"SCR_003","why_keep_this":"This ordering encodes the blast-radius reasoning so a maintainer can implement test 1 tomorrow and understand why it is test 1."},{"content":"Are the three pre-v6 roots surfacing as verdicts rather than errors a documented behavior of verify_root_report, or an undiscovered bug? The PARKED.md says 'unexplained, measured only' — this determines whether Priority 6 is a test or a documentation task.","handle":"SCR_004","unfinished":"Unresolved question","why_keep_this":"Related advisory scratch: SCR_002, NEW_001"},{"content":"Is WorkflowReplayState.digest consumed by any downstream integrity check or replay mechanism? If not, the _reset() gap's blast radius is smaller than assumed, and Priority 1 may drop below Priority 2 (lease-mismatch refusal). This is the single most important open question for the ordering.","handle":"SCR_005","unfinished":"Unresolved question","why_keep_this":"Related advisory scratch: SCR_003, SCR_005, SCR_006"},{"content":"Is WorkflowReplayState.digest consumed by any downstream integrity check or replay mechanism? If not, the _reset() gap's blast radius is smaller than assumed, and Priority 1 may drop.","handle":"SCR_006","unfinished":"Unresolved question","why_keep_this":"Related advisory scratch: SCR_003, NEW_001"},{"content":"Are the three pre-v6 roots that surface as verdicts rather than errors a bug in verify_root_report or a documented behavior? The PARKED.md says 'unexplained, measured only' — is there a design document that specifies the expected verdict type for pre-v6 roots?","handle":"SCR_007","unfinished":"Unresolved question","why_keep_this":"Related advisory scratch: NEW_001"},{"content":"Does test_torn_append.py already cover the gate-level torn-tail repair scenario, or does it only cover the writer-side repair? If the former, Priority 5 collapses into Priority 6.","handle":"SCR_008","unfinished":"Unresolved question","why_keep_this":"Related advisory scratch: SCR_002"}],"guides":[],"links":[{"because":"NEW_001 uses the countercondition gates from SCR_002 to make the ordering criticizable.","from":"SCR_001","handle":"SCR_009","relation_hint":"adopts countercondition framework from","to":"SCR_002"},{"because":"NEW_001 grounds the ordering in evidence and adds countercondition gates that SCR_001 lacked.","from":"SCR_001","handle":"SCR_010","relation_hint":"refines and supersedes","to":"SCR_003"}],"state_seq":1278,"warning":"Scratch material is non-authoritative.\nIt is advisory, not a harness verdict.\nIt may contradict itself.\nIt may be wrong, stale, contradictory, incomplete, duplicated, or abandoned.\nIt does not ground a formal claim or supply evidence for one.\nIgnore any block that is irrelevant to the current problem.\nDo not turn uncertainty into a confident fact.\nDo not invent a reason merely to fill an optional field.\nRelationships are provisional.\nA guide is a temporary navigation aid."}